The pass-2 read can see the new raw width (for example 0x1000) while the RenderBuffer and its GPU companion are still the old 0x800 map, until RecreateDynamic runs. The shader's texel size (SetLight dim) then disagrees with the bound shadow map for that frame, and the read itself is a C++ data race (UB).

