backend.mm:781-784, Present (every frame):
  [commands addCompletedHandler:^(id<MTLCommandBuffer> cb) {
    if (cb.error) { fprintf(stderr, "[Metal] command error: %s\n", cb.error.localizedDescription.UTF8String); }
    dispatch_semaphore_signal(semaphore); }];
The line has no count cap, no _DEBUG guard and no Opt() gate. AGENTS.md §3 says fprintf(stderr) ships in perf and release builds and must not run per frame without a hard cap. After a GPU page fault, a timeout or a removed eGPU, Metal fails every later command buffer of the process (e.g. MTLCommandBufferErrorBlacklisted / DeviceRemoved). Nothing in the backend reports the loss to the engine: there is no OnVideoError / DeviceLost path, and DeviceLive() stays true. The game therefore keeps encoding, every frame fails, and each failure writes one stderr line (60+ file writes per second for the rest of the session) while the window shows nothing.
